{"content":[{"c":["MIZPAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Name meaning “watchtower” in Hebrew (alternately spelled Mizpeh) used to designate a number of different locations mentioned in the OT and Apocrypha."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Place in Gilead where Jacob and Laban made a covenant (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.31.49","r":"Gen.31.49","rawR":"Gen.31.49","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.31.49","value":"Gen.31.49"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 31:49"},") and set up a heap of stones to mark the borders between their territories."],"sourceClass":"list-space","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Place referred to as “the land of Mizpah” (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.11.3","r":"Josh.11.3","rawR":"Josh.11.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.11.3","value":"Josh.11.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 11:3"},") or the “valley of Mizpah” (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.11.8","r":"Josh.11.8","rawR":"Josh.11.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.11.8","value":"Josh.11.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 11:8"},") near Mt Hermon and inhabited by the Hivites."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Town in Judah near Lachish referred to in ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.15.38","r":"Josh.15.38","rawR":"Josh.15.38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.15.38","value":"Josh.15.38"}],"t":"ref","v":"Joshua 15:38"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Place in the tribal area of Benjamin (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.18.26","r":"Josh.18.26","rawR":"Josh.18.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.18.26","value":"Josh.18.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 18:26"},"). It was here that the Israelites gathered to war against the tribe of Benjamin (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.20.1","r":"Judg.20.1","rawR":"Judg.20.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.20.1","value":"Judg.20.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 20:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Judg.21.1","r":"Judg.21.1","rawR":"Judg.21.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.21.1","value":"Judg.21.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:1"},") after the men of Gibeah had abused and killed the concubine of a visiting Levite. It was here that Samuel called all Israel together to pray for victory over the Philistines (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.7.5-8","r":"1Sam.7.5-8","rawR":"1Sam.7.5-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.7.5-8","value":"1Sam.7.5-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 7:5-8"},"). Later, Samuel called for an assembly at Mizpah to publicly designate Saul as king and to instruct the people and king in the ways of the kingdom (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.10.17-25","r":"1Sam.10.17-25","rawR":"1Sam.10.17-25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.10.17-25","value":"1Sam.10.17-25"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:17-25"},"). In the time of Asa, Mizpah was a fortified town on the border between Israel and Judah (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.15.22","r":"1Kgs.15.22","rawR":"1Kgs.15.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.15.22","value":"1Kgs.15.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 15:22"},"). After the fall of Jerusalem in 586 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," to the Babylonians, Mizpah became the residence of Gedaliah the governor (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.25.23-24","r":"2Kgs.25.23-24","rawR":"2Kgs.25.23-24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.25.23-24","value":"2Kgs.25.23-24"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 25:23-24"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.40.10","r":"Jer.40.10","rawR":"Jer.40.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.40.10","value":"Jer.40.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 40:10"},"), who was murdered there by Ishmael of the “royal seed” (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.41.3","r":"Jer.41.3","rawR":"Jer.41.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.41.3","value":"Jer.41.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 41:3"},"). Two days later Ishmael murdered a company of pilgrims who were going to Jerusalem to bring their offerings at the ruined temple, and he cast their bodies into a cistern that had been constructed centuries earlier by Asa."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["In the intertestamental period Mizpah continued to be an important religious center. Judas Maccabeus called the people together at Mizpah “because Israel formerly had a place of prayer in Mizpah” (",{"href":"?bref=1Macc.3.46","r":"1Macc.3.46","rawR":"1Macc.3.46","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Macc.3.46","value":"1Macc.3.46"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Macc 3:46"},")."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"},{"c":["5. Home of Jephthah, from which he led the Israelites in battle against the Ammonites, and to which he returned to carry out his vow (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.10.1-11.40","r":"Judg.10.1-11.40","rawR":"Judg.10.1-11.40","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.10.1-11.40","value":"Judg.10.1-11.40"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 10–11"},"). This is possibly the same place as the Ramath-mizpeh of ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.13.26","r":"Josh.13.26","rawR":"Josh.13.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.13.26","value":"Josh.13.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Joshua 13:26"}," and is thought by many to be identified with Khirbat Jal’ad just south of the Jabbok."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["6. Town in Moab to which David fled from Saul (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.22.3","r":"1Sam.22.3","rawR":"1Sam.22.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.22.3","value":"1Sam.22.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 22:3"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Mizpah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 31:49","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.31.49","rawQueryValue":"Gen.31.49","sourceRefExact":"Gen.31.49"},{"anchorText":"Jos 11:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.11.3","rawQueryValue":"Josh.11.3","sourceRefExact":"Josh.11.3"},{"anchorText":"Jos 11:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.11.8","rawQueryValue":"Josh.11.8","sourceRefExact":"Josh.11.8"},{"anchorText":"Joshua 15:38","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.15.38","rawQueryValue":"Josh.15.38","sourceRefExact":"Josh.15.38"},{"anchorText":"Jos 18:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.18.26","rawQueryValue":"Josh.18.26","sourceRefExact":"Josh.18.26"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 20:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.20.1","rawQueryValue":"Judg.20.1","sourceRefExact":"Judg.20.1"},{"anchorText":"21:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.21.1","rawQueryValue":"Judg.21.1","sourceRefExact":"Judg.21.1"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 7:5-8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.7.5-8","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.7.5-8","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.7.5-8"},{"anchorText":"10:17-25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.10.17-25","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.10.17-25","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.10.17-25"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 15:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.15.22","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.15.22","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.15.22"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 25:23-24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.25.23-24","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.25.23-24","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.25.23-24"},{"anchorText":"Jer 40:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.40.10","rawQueryValue":"Jer.40.10","sourceRefExact":"Jer.40.10"},{"anchorText":"Jer 41:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.41.3","rawQueryValue":"Jer.41.3","sourceRefExact":"Jer.41.3"},{"anchorText":"1 Macc 3:46","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Macc.3.46","rawQueryValue":"1Macc.3.46","sourceRefExact":"1Macc.3.46"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 10–11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.10.1-11.40","rawQueryValue":"Judg.10.1-11.40","sourceRefExact":"Judg.10.1-11.40"},{"anchorText":"Joshua 13:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.13.26","rawQueryValue":"Josh.13.26","sourceRefExact":"Josh.13.26"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 22:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.22.3","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.22.3","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.22.3"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"9bb407ab295709296077af9368250719f356b95daeb181bde5722b5fed1cbe8a","sourceItemName":"Mizpah","sourceItemOrder":370,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Mizpah","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Mizpah","title":"Mizpah","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}